<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Security groups for gdrive_odoo_sync (SPEC §7.1).

    Three groups, strictly nested, each one a superset of the last:

        group_gdrive_user     implies base.group_user
        group_gdrive_manager  implies group_gdrive_user
        group_gdrive_admin    implies group_gdrive_manager

    Category is base.module_category_productivity (SPEC §7.1), so Odoo renders
    the trio as a single "Google Drive Sync" selector on the user form rather
    than as three independent checkboxes — which is what the strict nesting
    means anyway, and stops an administrator from creating the nonsensical
    "manager but not user" combination by hand.

    WHY three groups and not two: the interesting boundary in this module is
    not "can see" vs "can configure", it is *"can author a mapping"* vs
    *"can execute a plan that writes to res.partner"*. A manager who builds and
    enables a mapping is doing normal, reversible configuration work. An
    administrator who applies a heal plan is mutating live business records,
    possibly soft-deleting them. Collapsing those two into one group means the
    person who writes the mapping is also the person who approves its
    consequences, which removes the only human checkpoint the system has.

    Note that ACL alone is NOT the guard on plan application: gdrive.plan's
    action_apply() additionally calls
    self.env.user.has_group('gdrive_odoo_sync.group_gdrive_admin') in Python.

    Managers are READ-ONLY on gdrive.plan and gdrive.plan.action. They used to
    hold write+create on both, nominally "only so the heal wizard can toggle
    each line's `selected` flag" — but Odoo ACLs are per MODEL, not per field.
    Blanket write let the role that is explicitly forbidden from applying plans
    rewrite an admin-approved plan before the admin executed it: change an
    action's res_model to res.users, its res_id to 2 and its payload to
    {'active': False}, or add new actions outright, and the apply fingerprints
    (drive version, drive mtime, Odoo row count, max write_date, both dataset
    hashes) cover none of it — they describe the *data*, not the plan's own
    action rows. Write on gdrive.plan itself additionally exposed `state` and
    `dry_run`, i.e. self-approval and disarming the dry run.

    The heal wizard's per-line `selected` toggle therefore belongs on its own
    transient line model (gdrive.heal.wizard.line, which managers do own), never
    on the persistent gdrive.plan.action rows an admin is about to execute.

    Credential entry (the service-account JSON) is gated more narrowly still,
    with groups="base.group_system" on the res.config.settings field — a
    gdrive administrator manages the sync, but only a system administrator
    handles a bearer credential for someone's entire Google Drive.

    This file loads FIRST in __manifest__.py's data list, because both
    ir.model.access.csv and gdrive_record_rules.xml reference these xml ids.
-->
<odoo>

    <record id="group_gdrive_user" model="res.groups">
        <field name="name">Google Drive Sync / User</field>
        <field name="category_id" ref="base.module_category_productivity"/>
        <field name="implied_ids" eval="[(4, ref('base.group_user'))]"/>
        <field name="comment">Read-only consumer of the sync. Browses mirrored Drive nodes and their
attachments, datasets, staged rows, verifications and drift findings.
Changes no configuration and triggers no run.</field>
    </record>

    <record id="group_gdrive_manager" model="res.groups">
        <field name="name">Google Drive Sync / Manager</field>
        <field name="category_id" ref="base.module_category_productivity"/>
        <field name="implied_ids" eval="[(4, ref('gdrive_odoo_sync.group_gdrive_user'))]"/>
        <field name="comment">Authors promotion mappings, edits scope rules, triggers discovery/staging runs
and previews heal plans. Explicitly CANNOT apply a plan: previewing is
non-mutating, applying writes to live business records.</field>
    </record>

    <record id="group_gdrive_admin" model="res.groups">
        <field name="name">Google Drive Sync / Administrator</field>
        <field name="category_id" ref="base.module_category_productivity"/>
        <field name="implied_ids" eval="[(4, ref('gdrive_odoo_sync.group_gdrive_manager'))]"/>
        <field name="comment">Manages connections, approves and applies heal plans, and is the only role that
may enable auto_heal. Entering the service-account key itself additionally
requires Settings / Technical (base.group_system).</field>
    </record>

    <!--
        The Odoo super-user is put in the administrator group so a fresh install
        is immediately usable by whoever installed it. Every other user starts
        with no gdrive group at all: with no ACL row matching them they simply
        do not see the menus — the correct default for a tool that can rewrite
        res.partner.
    -->
    <record id="base.user_admin" model="res.users">
        <field name="groups_id" eval="[(4, ref('gdrive_odoo_sync.group_gdrive_admin'))]"/>
    </record>

</odoo>
